mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I normally do not like opening balanced hands with 11 HCP as they usually do not meet the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at|. However, when making |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| calculations I like to use ^*BBergen Adjusted Points^*n to figure out how many points a hand is worth.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Admittedly, using raw HCP the hand does not meet the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at|. But when you add one point for the quality diamond suit and one point for 4 aces and tens and only one jack using ^*BBergen Adjusted Points^*n the hand is actually worth 13 points and definitely meets the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at|.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Further, as you noticed North opened 1@C with 4-4 in the minors. I have no problem with that, and in fact prefer to do so. Although many feel you should open 1@D with 4-4 in the minors, I don't happen to agree.|
PG| ***** 3 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|These days most players bypass diamonds to bid a major and here they would respond 1@S with my hand. My style is to bid 1@D if I have a decent hand and if I have a weak hand I would bypass the diamonds and bid my major--1@S here|
PG| ***** 4 ***** |


.
mb|1D|mb|P|mb|2D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The double is now takeout for the majors. But East might have considered doubling the first time. I do not have a problem either with pass or double the first round. However, it is always better to get into the auction as early as possible, so it would have been better for East to have doubled over 1@C rather than delaying making the double until the second round of bidding.|
PG| ***** 5 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Let me repeat, the auction by East was reasonable. However, to be consistent East might as well have doubled the first time or passed the second time.|
PG| ***** 6 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The hand didn't essentially change after the 2nd round of bidding. Therefore, if you choose to double it is better to do it earlier than later.|
PG| ***** 7 ***** |


