nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kib: ^*NWas it possible to make 3 hearts?|
PG| ***** 21 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Yes. West should play North for the @CK and @C10. So, at trick eight while W/E have four tricks, when West leads the @C8 and North plays low. Declarer should also play low and that wins. The way West played the hand, the only way to avoid a club trick is for North to have the doubleton @CK.|
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Given the auction, where North opened 1@C and then raised diamonds, North is known to have at least 4 clubs. Therefore, the doubleton @CK onside is not possible. Let me back track and show you.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


