cp|8|AT|
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As it turns out, yes. But I did not know that, and with 2 aces and partner bidding 2@C, which shows at least 10 points we can't let them play in 5@S undoubled. |
PG| ***** 55 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|One problem is partner was a little weak for his 2@C bid although it probably doesn't matter. North should be able to figure out the third diamond is not cashing because I bid 5@C after opening 1@D. So it is almost certain I have 5 diamonds. I might have 5 clubs in which case a club is no better but it might not.|
PG| ***** 56 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That was a little unlucky for us. The heart hook worked for them and partner had nothing in hearts. |
PG| ***** 57 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It turns out that unless they lead a heart we would make 6@C because say they lead a spade I ruff, draw trump and run diamonds to discard 2 hearts from dummy and end up losing only one heart. |
PG| ***** 58 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|A very interesting hand where both sides can make a lot of tricks.|
PG| ***** 59 ***** |


