qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   April 10, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,danpsych,aspiring|
md|1SJ87HAQ932DJT54C5,SAKQ6532HJ85DQCK2,ST9HT76DAK9762CT4,S4HK4D83CAQJ98763|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|1S|mb|2D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North is a little weak for 2@D. The hand should have 10 HCP or so or at least be a little less flat. For example, if North's distribution was 6-3-3-1, I might bid 3@D with his hand especially at this favorable vulnerability.|
PG| ***** 61 ***** |


mb|3C|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Notwithstanding the weakness of North's hand, I have a clear |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| 3@D bid. The ^*BLAW^*n must be your guideline on all competitive auctions.|
PG| ***** 62 ***** |


mb|4S|mb|P?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East is not happy with 4@S. The 4@S here is what I call ^*BI didn't ask for your opinion partner^*n bid. So East must pass.|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 64 ***** |


