up|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I did what is called a ^*BPseudo Squeeze^*n meaning I didn't really have a squeeze. But often when you have all the tricks but one, and you cash them all. |
PG| ***** 98 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The defenders will make a discarding mistake as they did here. In double dummy East can figure out to save the club and throw the @HA, though it is hard to do that. |
PG| ***** 99 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As to why East ducked the first heart that was 100% correct. playing @HJ means that West does not hold the @HQ. So had East played the @HA, then both my @HQ and @HK are good and I can throw a losing club on the @HQ.|
PG| ***** 100 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Aces are made to cover the other side's honors when possible. So the duck was correct. And had East figured out, not easy to do, saving a club and discard a heart it would not have cost a trick. Not to mention had West lead a 2nd heart, it would not cost a trick either.|
PG| ***** 101 ***** |


